embed_string(): copy the overlay word with memcpy().

The function overlays a distribution word inside an already-populated
fixed-width field, intentionally without a NUL terminator.
strncpy(dest, word, strlen(word)) does exactly that, but matches the
classic truncation-bug pattern and trips -Wstringop-truncation.
memcpy() of strlen(word) bytes is byte-for-byte identical for
non-overlapping buffers and carries no string semantics for the
compiler to second-guess.

No behavior change: item.dat is byte-identical.  (History: two earlier
attempts to silence this warning corrupted i_manager_id and truncated
i_formulation; see the dbt7 ChangeLog.)

Index: dbt7/dsgen/tools/build_support.c
===================================================================
--- dbt7.orig/dsgen/tools/build_support.c
+++ dbt7/dsgen/tools/build_support.c
@@ -369,7 +369,7 @@ embed_string(char *szDest, char *szDist,
 
 	pick_distribution(&szWord, szDist, nValue, nWeight, nStream);
 	nPosition = genrand_integer(NULL, DIST_UNIFORM, 0, strlen(szDest) - strlen(szWord) - 1, 0, nStream);
-	strncpy(&szDest[nPosition], szWord, strlen(szWord));
+	memcpy(&szDest[nPosition], szWord, strlen(szWord));
 
 	return(0);
 }
